{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kf3X2fdDUi5BPJRQfWVbA1","type":"tool_result","content":"# ContamCal Experiment Plan\n# Each experiment maps to Core Claims in paper_framing.md\n# Priority: P0 = must-run, P1 = important, P2 = bonus\n\nexperiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # P0: Core experiments — must complete for submission\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - id: exp-001\n    name: controlled_sft_injection\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      SFT contamination injection on Qwen2.5-0.5B/1.5B/3B at 5 dosage levels\n      (0%, 5%, 25%, 50%, 100% benchmark items as paraphrases in SFT data).\n      Produces ground-truth contaminated/clean model pairs. 15 SFT runs total\n      (3 models × 5 dosages), parallelized across GPUs. 3 seeds per condition\n      for key metrics (mean ± std).\n      Paraphrase generation: use strong open LLM (Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct or\n      equivalent) with controlled semantic similarity — following methodology\n      of \"Rethinking Benchmark and Contamination\" (arXiv 2023). Target:\n      high semantic similarity (cosine >0.85) but low lexical overlap\n      (BLEU <0.3) to evade n-gram decontamination while preserving\n      contamination effect. Quality validation: automated similarity metrics\n      + human spot-check on 50 random pairs per benchmark.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 50\n    deps: []\n    benchmarks: [MMLU, GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HumanEval]\n    models: [Qwen2.5-0.5B, Qwen2.5-1.5B, Qwen2.5-3B]\n    seeds: 3\n    registry_id: exp_001_sft_d100_15B_v2\n    # Multi-run experiment; related registry entries:\n    # exp_001_sft_injection, exp_001_sft_0pct_05B (DONE), exp_001_sft_0pct_15B (DONE),\n    # exp_001_sft_0pct_3B, exp_001_sft_0pct_05B_s123, exp_001_sft_0pct_15B_s123,\n    # exp_001_sft_0pct_3B_s123, exp_001_sft_d100_05B (DONE), exp_001_sft_d005_05B (DONE),\n    # exp_001_eval_* (various)\n\n  - id: exp-002\n    name: stage1_signal_pipeline\n    claim: 2\n    description: >\n      Compute 4 detection signals on all contaminated + clean models from exp-001:\n      (a) embedding-based semantic retrieval (FAISS + sentence-transformers),\n      (b) Min-K%++ membership inference,\n      (c) ConStat performance gap (original vs paraphrased items),\n      (d) Self-Critique entropy collapse.\n      Output: per-model-item exposure scores for each signal.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 20","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9Qo3LdQTenn4vaDkbbYEr","session_id":"b63aa037-c95f-4d42-a996-1a4555dbde83","uuid":"8aa9fde1-c742-420c-94b6-3531cdf79322","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:26:11.614Z"}
