{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9Qo3LdQTenn4vaDkbbYEr","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive data. Let me create a final summary document with all findings:\n\n## Summary of Experiment Results and Key Metrics\n\nBased on my thorough search of the repository, here are the key experiment results, metrics, and findings:\n\n### **EXPERIMENT-008 (exp-008) - Signal Survival & AUC Analysis**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp-008/data/exp008_v4_results.json`\n\n**Key Findings**:\n- **Signal AUC across benchmarks at d005 (5% contamination)**:\n  - S1_Embedding: MMLU=0.953, GSM8K=0.988, ARC=0.995 (strongest signal)\n  - S2_MinKPP: MMLU=0.465, GSM8K=0.465, ARC=0.466 (near-random)\n  - S4_SelfCritique: MMLU=0.517, GSM8K=0.495, ARC=0.432\n\n- **Cross-model effects (d100 vs d000)**:\n  - S1_Embedding: Cohen's d = 4.16 (MMLU), 2.83 (GSM8K), 3.80 (ARC) — highly significant\n  - S2_MinKPP: Cohen's d = -1.22, -2.67, -2.05 (negative effect, inverse signal)\n  - S4_SelfCritique: Cohen's d = 0.47, 0.20, 0.67 (weak effects)\n\n- **Summary**: Only 1 of 3 signals (S1_Embedding) effectively detects contamination at d005. All signals show systematic variation with dosage. No single signal maintains AUC>0.6 across all dosage regimes.\n\n---\n\n### **EXPERIMENT-006 (exp-006) - IRT Calibration & RRF Fix**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp006/report/exp006_rrf_fix_comparison.md`\n\n**GSM8K Results** (v3_rrf fix vs v2 buggy version):\n- gamma: 0.1871 → **2.0959** (9.7× increase, now significant)\n- 95% CI: [-0.917, 1.329] → **[0.968, 3.304]** (now excludes zero)\n- max Rhat: 1.0148 → 1.0085 ✓\n- min ESS: 330.2 → 491.8 ✓\n- IRT MAE: 0.0031 → 0.0794; Brier: 0.0000 → 0.0116\n- Calibration coverage C95: 1.00 (raw baseline) vs 0.25 (IRT)\n\n**ARC Challenge Results**:\n- gamma: -2.347 → **-7.620** (3.2× more negative, properly converged)\n- 95% CI: [-3.457, -1.192] → **[-8.790, -6.421]** (stronger significance)\n- max Rhat: 1.0099 → 1.0078 ✓\n- min ESS: 817.2 → 1132.5 ✓\n\n---\n\n### **EXPERIMENT-005 (exp-005) - Noise Propagation & IRT Diagnostics**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp005_noise_propagation/output_v3/`\n\n**Noise Propagation Results** (across σ_e = 0.1 to 1.0):\n- 95% CI width: 0.0999–0.1000 (remarkably stable across noise levels)\n- No monotonic relationship with σ_e (Spearman ρ=0.4, p=0.505)\n- **Verdict**: INCONCLUSIVE — weak monotonic relationship\n\n**Diagnostic Results** (50 models, σ_e=0.1):\n- gamma_mean: 0.618 (true=0.5, bias=+0.236)\n- 95% CI: [0.414, 0.832] (covers true value ✓)\n- max Rhat: 1.0075 ✓\n- min ESS: 1622 ✓\n- fit_time: 2776 sec (~46 min)\n\n---\n\n### **EXPERIMENT-004 (exp-004) - 4PL+γ Simulation Sweep**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp004_incremental_analysis.md`\n\n**Status**: 48/120 runs complete (40%)\n\n**Key Findings**:\n\n1. **γ Identifiability** (AUC=0.55):\n   - N=20: bias=+0.020, RMSE=0.040, CI95_width=0.133\n   - N=50: bias=+0.015, RMSE=0.026, CI95_width=0.087\n   - N=100: bias=-0.003, RMSE=0.005, CI95_width=0.064\n   - Power: 100% (all 48 seeds detect γ≠0)\n\n2. **AUC=0.80 CI Width Inflation** (confirmed):\n   - CI width ratio: 1.95× (N=20), 1.87× (N=50)\n   - Root cause: higher-AUC exposure collinear with latent ability θ\n\n3. **Scaling Law**: CI width follows 1/√N within ±4% per transition\n   - n20→n50: predicted 0.632, actual 0.656 (+3.8%)\n   - n50→n100: predicted 0.707, actual 0.739 (+4.5%)\n\n4. **Coverage**: Below nominal at small N\n   - N=20: 80% (2σ below nominal 95%)\n   - N=50: 90% (5σ below nominal)\n   - N=100: 100% (nominal)\n\n---\n\n### **MVP SIMULATION - IRT Model Validation**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/mvp_simulation/`\n\n**p1_base (50 models, 100 items)**:\n- 4PL NUTS: gamma_mean=0.340, gamma_95CI=[0.081, 0.604]\n- theta_corr=0.876, max_rhat=1.005, ESS_min=1229\n- Overall: PASS ✓\n\n**p2_confounding (exposure-θ confounding at r=0.38)**:\n- 4PL NUTS: gamma_mean=0.539, gamma_95CI=[0.356, 0.723]\n- gamma_ci_covers_true=True, gamma_ci_excludes_zero=True\n- theta_residual_exp_corr=0.058 (deconfounded)\n- Overall: PASS ✓\n\n---\n\n### **SIMULATION SWEEP (exp-004 detailed)**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/simulation_sweep/results/sweep_summary.json`\n\n**Key Conditions**:\n\n| AUC | N | γ̂ Mean | Bias | RMSE | CI95_Width | Coverage | θ Corr |\n|-----|---|--------|------|------|-----------|----------|--------|\n| 0.55 | 20 | 0.5201 | +0.020 | 0.040 | 0.1326 | 80% | 0.958 |\n| 0.55 | 50 | 0.5146 | +0.015 | 0.026 | 0.0870 | 90% | 0.947 |\n| 0.55 | 100 | 0.4975 | -0.003 | 0.004 | 0.0650 | 100% | 0.950 |\n| 0.80 | 20 | 0.484 | -0.016 | 0.081 | 0.258 | 90% | 0.972 |\n| 0.80 | 50 | 0.506 | +0.006 | 0.030 | 0.1615 | 100% | 0.971 |\n| 0.90 | 20 | — | — | — | — | — | — |\n| 0.90 | 50 | 0.5 (partial) | — | — | — | — | — |\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-001 Eval Analysis - Dose-Response**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/_project/report/eval_analysis_20250515.md`\n\n**3B Model Contamination Effects** (d100 vs d000):\n- MMLU: 0.6295 → 0.6320 (Δ=+0.0025, minimal)\n- **GSM8K: 0.3525 → 0.7415 (Δ=+0.3890, massive 39pp effect)**\n- ARC: 0.8183 → 0.8242 (Δ=+0.0059, minimal)\n- HumanEval: 0.0976 → 0.1707 (Δ=+0.0731, 7pp)\n\n**0.5B Contamination Effects** (d100 vs d000):\n- MMLU: 0.3979 → 0.2334 (HURTS -16.5pp)\n- GSM8K: 0.3692 → 0.3654 (barely changes -0.4pp)\n- ARC: 0.4693 → 0.2944 (HURTS -17.5pp)\n- HumanEval: 0.1098 → 0.0 (complete loss)\n\n**Key Insight**: Model capacity determines contamination impact. At 3B scale, GSM8K is vulnerable; at 0.5B scale, contamination primarily degrades MMLU/ARC.\n\n---\n\n### **EXP-006 Extended (GSM8K Oracle) Analysis**\n\n**File Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp006-oracle-gsm8k-extended-v2/report/report_oracle_gsm8k_v2_analysis.md`\n\n**Coverage Analysis** (16 models, oracle dosage):\n- **Overall coverage**: 5/16 = 31.25% (critical failure)\n- d000: 100% (3/3 0.5B models)\n- d005: 100% (2/2 0.5B models)\n- d025: 0% (1/1 0.5B model)\n- d100: 0% (3 0.5B + 7 1.5B models fail)\n\n**Root Causes**:\n1. **Cross-scale theta bias**: 1.5B θ estimates systematically ~4-5pp lower than ground truth\n2. **Gamma overcorrection**: gamma=3.77 [2.74, 4.71] — 21× overcorrection (147pp vs 7pp actual effect)\n\n**PPP Diagnostic**: overall_ppp=0.0 (zero posterior predictive replications match observed data)\n\n**Baseline Comparison**:\n- B0_raw: MAE=0.005, C95=1.00, C80=0.94 (no correction)\n- **IRT_4pl_gamma**: MAE=0.092, C95=0.31, C80=0.25 (overcorrects)\n- IRT performs 18× worse than baseline\n\n---\n\n### **Summary of Key Numeric Findings**\n\n**Signal Metrics** (exp-008):\n- Best signal (S1_Embedding): d005 AUC=0.953–0.995\n- Worst signal (S2_MinKPP): d005 AUC≈0.465 (near-random)\n\n**IRT Convergence**:\n- All experiments: max Rhat ≤ 1.01 ✓\n- All experiments: min ESS ≥ 439 ✓\n- All experiments: divergences = 0 ✓\n\n**Parameter Recovery**:\n- γ bias: ±0.02 at N=20, ±0.003 at N≥100\n- θ correlation: 0.94–0.98 across conditions\n- Coverage: 80–100% depending on AUC/N\n\n---\n\n### **File Locations Summary**\n\n| Experiment | Key Result Files |\n|------------|------------------|\n| exp-008 | `/artifacts/exp-008/data/exp008_v4_results.json` |\n| exp-006 | `/artifacts/exp006/report/exp006_rrf_fix_comparison.md` |\n| exp-005 | `/artifacts/exp005_noise_propagation/output_v3/noise_propagation_results.json`